==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|lugar}}, {{m|roa-opt|logar}}, from {{inh|pt|LL.|localis|locālis, locālem|local}}, from {{inh|pt|la|locus||place}}, from {{der|pt|la|stlocus}}, from {{der|pt|ine-pro|*stel-||to put}}. {{doublet|pt|local}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|/lu.ˈɣaɾ/|lang=pt}}
** {{audio|Pt-lugar.oga|Audio|lang=pt}}
* {{a|Brazil}} {{IPA|/lu.ˈɡaʁ/|lang=pt}}
** {{a|Paulista}} {{IPA|[lu.ˈɡaɾ]|[lu.ˈɡaɹ]|lang=pt}}
** {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|[lu.ˈɡaɾ]|[lu.ˈɡaɻ]|lang=pt}}
** {{a|Carioca}} {{IPA|[lu.ˈɡaχ]|lang=pt}}

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|m|es}}

# {{senseid|pt|location}} {{l|en|place}} {{gloss|location or position}}
#: {{ux|pt|Não vamos a Camelot, é um '''lugar''' bobo.|t=Let’s not go to Camelot, it’s a silly '''place'''.}}
# {{senseid|pt|available room}} {{l|en|available}} {{l|en|room}}
#: {{ux|pt|Há '''lugar''' para cinco pessoas neste carro.|t=There is '''room''' for five people in this car.}}
# {{senseid|pt|position in a rank}} {{l|en|place}} {{gloss|position within a rank}}
#: {{ux|pt|Quem fica em primeiro '''lugar''' ganha medalha de ouro.|t=He who gets first '''place''' earns gold medals.}}
# {{senseid|pt|opportunity}} {{lb|pt|uncountable}} {{l|en|opportunity}} {{gloss|chance for advancement, progress or profit}}
#: {{ux|pt|Não dê '''lugar''' à corrupção.|t=Leave no '''space''' for corruption.}}
#: {{ux|pt|Não tive '''lugar''' para terminar o serviço.|t=I didn’t have '''an opportunity''' to finish the job.}}
# {{senseid|pt|available seat}} a {{l|en|reserved}} or {{l|en|available}} {{l|en|seat}}
#: {{ux|pt|Teremos que comer em outro lugar, aqui não há mais '''lugares'''.|t=We will have to eat elsewhere, there are no '''seats left''' here.}}
# {{senseid|pt|position in a medium}} a {{l|en|position}} in a {{l|en|book}}, {{l|en|song}} or {{l|en|film}}
#: {{ux|pt|Parei de ler o livro naquele '''lugar'''.|t=I stopped reading the book on that '''spot'''.}}

